{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And there did not arise a prophet again in Israel like Moses.</b> No prophet attained the level of his prophecy. From this it follows that no prophet is authorized to introduce anything new from now on, as they said: \">A court cannot annul the words of a fellow court unless it is greater than it in wisdom and in number\" (Shabbat 104a).\"" "<b>Whom HaShem knew.</b> The prophet acquires an accession of intellectual light without doubt through the light of the King's face when he prophesies, as it says: וְהִתְנַבִּיתָ עִמָּהֶם וְנֶהְפַּכְתָּ לְאִישׁ אַחֵר (1 Samuel 10:6). Therefore, when He declared the lovingkindness of El upon His people, He said: וָאָקִים מִבְּנֵיכֶם לִנְבִיאִים (Amos 2:11). And since the entire activity of the blessed El is through His knowledge of Himself alone, He said אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ to indicate that He acted upon him through His knowing, for his good — as in מָה אָדָם וַתֵּדָעֵהוּ (Psalms 144:3), וָאֵדָעֲךָ בְשֵׁם (Exodus 33:17), וַיֵּדַע אֱלֹהִים (Exodus 2:25), יוֹדֵעַ ה׳ דֶּרֶךְ צַדִּיקִים (Psalms 1:6), and many others besides these." "<b>Face to face.</b> While he was yet using his senses."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The Talmudic citation is from b. Shabbat 23b / Eruvin 62b in standard numbering; Sforno's reference to שבת ק\"ד likely reflects a variant pagination."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:50.534212519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}